.TH "GIT-WORK" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-work's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-work-migrate - Migrate the store once from git-bug's format to the owned model


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work migrate [--dry-run] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Migrate the store once from git-bug's format to the owned model (bf6f392).

.PP
Every issue under refs/issues/* is replayed under refs/work-issues/\fI,
one commit per original commit, with its id, its comment ids and its
lamport times unchanged, and the label taxonomy becomes fields;
the identities are copied to refs/work-users/\fP\&. The old refs are kept.

.PP
The schema has to be in place first: git work schema import schema.yaml.
The command refuses when refs/work-issues/* holds anything.
doc/design/store-migration.md is the design.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print what would be written and write nothing but the identity copy

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for migrate


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work(1)\fP
